docs/phase-1-plan.md:52:Phase 2 columns present now so `orders`/`order_proposals` never need a shape change: `parent_order_id`, `replaces_order_id`, `order_proposal_id`, `submission_unknown` state, `submission_attempts`, `guardrail_results`, `risk_rule_version`, `acknowledged_warnings`, `kind`/`target_order_id` for stop adjustments.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:94:**Schwab client:** built to `docs/schwab-api-contract.md`. Net::HTTP; plaintext account numbers scrubbed inside the client before any body is returned; logs carry path templates (`/accounts/{hash}/orders`), never hashes, bodies, or headers; one time helper for the three input and three output formats; `BigDecimal` for every money and quantity value; a shared Solid Cache rate budget of 100 requests/minute across Puma and the worker; retries on 429, 5xx, and transport errors for GETs and the refresh grant only (1, 4, 16 s with jitter, `Retry-After` capped at 60 s), never on 4xx; one refresh-and-retry on a 401. Error classes: `AuthError`, `ReauthRequired`, `RateLimited`, `ServerError`, `RequestError`, `TransportError`, `UnknownOutcome` (non-idempotent calls only, chosen by HTTP method), `MappingError`. Interface adds `order(hash, order_id)` so working stops older than the lookback are re-fetched by id, and `instrument(symbol_or_cusip)` for identity fallback. Mappers return `Data` structs with a scrubbed `raw` member; jobs never see a Schwab field name. `Schwab::FakeClient` sits below the mappers and returns raw-shaped hashes with a scriptable per-call queue. Sync runs can finish `partial` with an `unmapped_values` count when individual records are quarantined.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:100:`app/models/agent/tools/*` each subclasses `Agent::Tool` and declares, with the `tool` macro, a `description`, `input` properties plus a `required` list, an `output` schema (every key required unless listed in `output_optional`, `additionalProperties: false` on both schemas), `call(**args)`, and permission metadata: `read_only`, `mcp`, `scheduled`. The tool's wire name is derived from the class name (`GetPortfolio` is `get_portfolio`). The MCP server registers tools where `mcp`; the scheduled runtime passes only tools where `scheduled && read_only`, enforced in one place (and at class-definition time: an unattended tool that is not read-only fails eager load) so a Phase 2 write tool cannot reach an unattended run by omission. `Agent::Tools.call(name, arguments, transport:)` is the one entry point for both transports: it validates the arguments against the input schema with the gem's validator (so the scheduled runtime gets the same gate the MCP gem applies), invokes the tool, normalizes every failure into a `Result` (`value`, `error`, `retry_after`, `ok?`, `text`), and writes the `tool_calls` row for every call including a denied one (an unknown tool and a tool the transport may not use are recorded and reported differently). Tools raise `Agent::Tool::InvalidArguments` for what the schema cannot express; any other exception is reported under the tool's name and returned as a tool error.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:105:| `get_account_health` | Equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from HWM (index-based), unprotected count, token status and age, last sync per feed, shadow mode, halt state, sync pause reason |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:110:| `get_risk_rules` | `available: false, rules: []` in Phase 1; reads no rows until the guardrail engine exists |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:114:**MCP server (revised after the step 8 counselors review).** `McpController < ActionController::API` at `match "/mcp", via: [post, get, delete]`: a `before_action` checks the bearer (`Bearer` scheme only, case-insensitive; `secure_compare`; never logged) and answers 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="invalid_token"` and a one-line JSON body, no HTML page and no `resource_metadata` (that would send Claude looking for an authorization server that does not exist). The action builds `MCP::Server` from the registry and hands the request to the gem's `StreamableHTTPTransport` with `stateless: true`, `enable_json_response: true`, `serve_subscriptions_listen: false`, `dns_rebinding_protection: false` (Rails host authorization owns the Host check; feeding the gem `request.host` would have it match the header against itself), and `max_request_bytes` well under the 4 MiB default (Rails parses the JSON body for its log line before the gem's cap runs, so the nginx `client_max_body_size` in §9 is the real first guard); the transport handles GET, DELETE, the protocol-version header, notifications (202), and both the 2025 handshake and the 2026-07-28 stateless transport. Rails `rate_limit to: 60, within: 1.minute` on the controller; JSON only; no CORS. The server advertises only the `tools` capability. Tools return `MCP::Tool::Response` with `structured_content` plus a text block of the same JSON, `additionalProperties: false` and `required` on every input and output schema, `validate_tool_call_results` on outside production so schema drift fails a spec rather than a Claude session, a failed call carries `retry_after` in `_meta`, and annotations `read_only_hint: true, destructive_hint: false, idempotent_hint: true, open_world_hint: false`. Tool exceptions never reach the transport: one dispatch wrapper rescues, writes the `tool_calls` row in an `ensure`, and returns a tool error carrying only the Schwab error message. Quotes and price history are cached with a long expiry and their own `fetched_at`; age beyond the freshness window triggers a refetch and a failed refetch returns the old entry with `stale: true`; the tools draw on a 70/min ceiling of the shared Schwab budget (passed as `budget:` to `Schwab.client`, taken once per request inside the client) so a chatty session cannot starve sync, and a rate limit is a tool error with `retry_after`, never a sleep. `get_portfolio` and `get_account_health` wrap the `Dashboard` read model rather than re-deriving anything; outputs carry the `protection` enum, nil for unknown risk, decimal strings for money, ISO 8601 New York timestamps, and never a `raw` column, an account hash, or the user's email (accounts are labelled by role). `get_journal` paginates (`limit` 50 default, 200 max, `offset`, `include_legs` off by default); `get_quotes` takes at most 50 symbols, reports `invalid_symbols` and `unavailable_symbols` (no fetch and nothing cached), answers only-invalid symbols as data rather than an outage, and raises the Schwab error only when nothing cached can stand in; `get_price_history` takes an enum range mapped to daily or weekly candles; `get_risk_rules` returns an empty list with `available: false` so the agent does not infer missing data. A spec walks every tool's serialized output for the account-hash pattern and `accountNumber`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:126:IRA and other read-only accounts sync positions and activities (for Phase 2 wash-sale checks) but never create trades. `Journal::BootstrapJob` and `Journal::LinkFillsJob` share one Solid Queue concurrency key per account, and every activity is linked in its own transaction: insert or find the leg by `activity_id`, recompute the trade as a pure function of its legs, then stamp `journaled_at` last. A rerun finds the existing leg and recomputes; it never skips because the activity was marked.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:186:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:213:- dokku app `athayde-desk` on gc2.meticulous.net (desk.athayde.com), postgres service `athayde-desk-db` linked (`DATABASE_URL`), letsencrypt issued. PRD §5.9's "Schwab app key/secret in dokku config vars" is superseded by decision 0.1: every secret is in `config/credentials/production.yml.enc` under `RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, and `config/initializers/credentials_check.rb` refuses a production boot with any of them missing (exempt during the image build, which runs with `SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY`). ENV holds only `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, `MEMORY_REPO_PATH`, `PORT`, and `RAILS_LOG_LEVEL`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:216:- `bin/dokku-setup`: idempotent and secret-free; run on the host as root in one SSH session (repeated connections trip fail2ban). It settles config vars, ports, `client-max-body-size 1m` (the MCP body cap does not depend on nginx's default), restart policy `unless-stopped` (the default gives up after ten crashes with no nag), stop timeout, the memory storage directory owned by uid 1000 and mounted read-only at `/rails/memory`, and prints the one-time steps: the first push (the `app.json` formation scales web=1 worker=1 on every deploy; `ps:scale` is refused while it exists), the memory clone with a read-only deploy key and its host cron, the postgres backup commands (PRD §5.9: `postgres:backup-auth`, `backup-set-encryption`, `backup-schedule "0 8 * * *"`, 08:00 UTC is 04:00 New York, clear of every job; `production.key` is kept with the dumps), the first-evening runbook, and the Claude connector header.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:233:8. MCP server + tool registry with permission metadata (decision 0.8 verified 2026-09-01: the connector dialog offers a request header).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:241:Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:251:**Deferred from the phase-level review (do before Phase 2, each gets more expensive weekly):** rename `Dashboard` to `Desk` (five consumers, one of them a screen) and `Agent::Run` to `Agent::Conversation`; fold `SystemStatus` onto the desk read model (halted_by, pause-since, last-sync-per-feed, and the token line are each written twice); one timestamp formatter per audience (the two locale formats for humans, `Agent.serialize` for machines; delete `Brief#stamp` and `Agent::Context#stamp`) and one cost label; move `Playwright::Scenario` to `lib/`; route `Agent::Context`'s setup stats through the registry or a shared method; add `audited` metadata to `Agent::Tool` for write tools; decide the activities policy when Schwab rejects one assumed type every run (today the run fails and re-backfills the window); `risk_rules` global uniqueness needs `NULLS NOT DISTINCT`; one trading account per desk (a validation collides with the factories; a partial unique index when Phase 2 needs it); `Instrument.lookup_cusip` can hit a token refresh inside the journal transaction (narrow); `Sync::CatchUpJob#perform` and the Playwright scenario loader have no Ruby-level specs; `Setup#avg_r` and `#expectancy` carry one number; the `market_hours` feed value is never written.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:259:- Which balance fields map to settled cash vs unsettled cash for a cash account.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:267:- Claude app custom connectors: static bearer header availability for this org (decision 0.8).
